+### Automatic RTX3090 storage and shell selection
+
+With no manual `BEAMZ_CUDA_*` overrides, `Simulation.compile()` automatically
+calibrates eligible RTX3090 programs on first use. It compares the three cyclic
+storage orders (`012`, `120`, `201`) and the existing `64x4` / `32x8` CPML shell
+tiles. The physical grid, 12-cell CPML, source/monitor sampling and FP32 precision
+remain unchanged. Existing automatic H/E fusion still applies within each layout;
+experimental CPML temporal blocking is not selected.
+
+Calibration uses a private initial state, exact complete-state validation against
+the branch's ordinary canonical layout, two additional warmups and six balanced
+timing rounds. Layout conversions are timed. A nondefault choice must reduce
+median runtime by at least 3% and win in both timing halves. This finds the best
+accepted member of a small candidate set, not a global optimum or a guarantee
+of beating another revision. First-use calibration adds setup time (about
+37 seconds in the initial 16.8-million-cell flat-domain check).
+
+Results persist under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/beamz/cuda-tuning` (otherwise
+`~/.cache/beamz/cuda-tuning`). Keys include the exact request, step count, native
+and Python solver fingerprints, JAX/platform versions, GPU UUID, driver and power
+limit. Configuration is stored in the returned immutable program and isolated
+in the compiled-program cache. A cache hit does not rerun the timing trials.
+
+```python
+program = sim.compile(num_steps=256, backend="cuda_streamed")
+from beamz.simulation.cuda.tuning import tuning_report
+print(program.config.cuda_storage_axes)
+print(tuning_report(program))  # choice, samples, rejections, cost and cache hit
+```
+
+`BEAMZ_CUDA_AUTOTUNE=off` disables selection. `refresh` recalibrates after clearing
+the program cache or starting a new process. `BEAMZ_CUDA_TUNING_CACHE` chooses a
+cache directory. Other explicit `BEAMZ_CUDA_*` overrides disable automatic
+selection, preserving manual experiments. Unwritable caches do not prevent runs.
+
+The initial automatic scope is one RTX3090, at least 8,388,608 logical cells,
+32–256 steps, uniform 3D lossless diagonal materials, CPML12, and native-compatible
+slab sources / DFT monitors. Other workloads retain existing dispatch. Calibration
+requires GPU telemetry, at least 4 GiB free memory between trials, and temperature
+below 85 C. It makes no power-limit changes. Decisions describe warm execution;
+startup cost can outweigh the gain for a simulation run only once. Calibration
+checks branch-internal parity; it does not resolve the separately recorded CPML
+numerical differences from `origin/main`.
